  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior experiments completed, there is zero evidence about which design axes (modality, encoder, profile, aggregation, fusion) matter most. The highest-priority uncertainty is establishing a clean performance floor. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the most minimal configuration in the search space: it uses a single modality (RNA), a single profile (no aggregation needed), and PCA (a deterministic, fast, well-understood encoder with no training variability). This isolates the raw RNA signal quality as a reference point. From this baseline, subsequent experiments can cleanly measure the incremental contribution of each design choice—adding multiprofile (config_002/003), swapping encoders (config_004/007), adding the image modality (config_016/022), or introducing aggregation and fusion—without confounding multiple variables. Choosing the simplest possible baseline first maximizes the interpretability of every future comparison and is the most information-efficient use of the first experiment under a limited budget."
}

